sec.p:
Sidechain χ1 dihedral angles (centered at -60°, +60°, and +180°) were monitored for each residue. The ±60° rotamers were treated as a single configurational state representing the state capable of forming backbone hydrogen bonds, while the +180° rotamer represented the non-bonding state. The free energy of the +180° rotamer (ΔGrot|i) for each residue i was calculated as:
ΔGrot∣i=−kBT⋅ln⁡(ci,180ci,−60+ci,+60) \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \Delta G_{r o t \mid i}=-k_{B} T \cdot \ln \left(\frac{c_{i, 180}}{c_{i,-60}+c_{i,+60}}\right)$$\end{document}
where c is the frame count for each state.
